# Austin 7 hp open two-seater, 1909-1911.
#
# The first Austin, introduced at the November 1909 Olympia show: a light
# 7 hp car. About 1,030 were built 1909-1911, of which 162 were Austin-badged.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austin_7_(1909)
#
# Dimensions 2.680 x 1.397 x about 1.55 m (height estimated), wheelbase
# 1.829 m (Culshaw and Horrobin, Complete Catalogue of British Cars).
#
# Shape reference: the side view is a 1909 period halftone, not a modern
# photograph. The front, rear and detail views are the 1910 Gaydon car
# BJ 1935, chassis 7058, engine 7064. The Commons description's 748 cc
# conflicts with the published 1,087/1,099 cc and is flagged in the notes.
#
# Colours: grade (d), no period UK document consulted. Black, Dark Green,
# Maroon and Grey are plain colour names. Weights 3, 2, 2, 1, total 8,
# provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 50 km/h. Comfort 18/357, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 18. Class 2.
# Dates 1909-1911 production, road tail staggered 1920-1922.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/austin-7-1909.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/austin-7-1909.dae. References:
# citycars/references/austin-7-1909/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the 1909 period halftone governs the profile; the 1910
# Gaydon car supplies the folded hood, fittings and lamp detail. The two are
# mixed and the mix is recorded. This is the only car of the five with a
# windscreen, and its glazing is pure black.


